From 26084bb76786fc28186ff0f31c4ccc3ebcdf3405 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:34:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tests): ignore clone capability work in SIGTERM copy
 fixture [daveey]

The locked page-copy fixture used the full .partial* cleanup inventory as
readiness. Since #3863, the clone capability probe briefly occupies that
namespace before the real destination exists. A readiness poll can return
that probe, then the assertion sees a live child and no staging file.

Explicitly disable clone only for this page-copy fixture, as the WAL copy
fixture already does. Preserve the real exclusive SQLite lock, SIGTERM
exit 143, empty stdout, and exhaustive staging cleanup assertions. No
production change, glob exclusion, retry adjustment or timeout widening.

Add a controlled owned-child regression: real _clone_unavailable creates
and removes its probe; socket barriers acknowledge its removal after the
parent observes it, then hold the child before actual staging. Replacing
only the filesystem clone makes the schedule independent of reflink
support. Removing the fixture opt-out reproduces the incident assertion.

Proof:
- Exact job 136812356125/run 44892881102 at 707a3bee7b61 downloaded
  with gh: readiness assertion (None is None and []), failed ID retry pass.
- Controlled old fixture RED at that exact assertion; fixed schedule GREEN.
- HERMES_TEST_FILE_RETRIES=0: targeted 2 pass; whole staging file 5 pass.
- Six backup files: 119 pass, 2 pre-existing progress index assertions fail,
  3 filesystem-dependent clone skips. Separate baseline repair owner
  t_e2f527f781935f35; production and progress test blobs unchanged here.
- scripts/hermes-python scripts/check --base origin/main: 21 checks OK.

Ownership: historical lock-deadline #342 and weakref/SystemExit #405
remain intact. Fresh hub open backup-owner SQL empty; open backup PR
search only unrelated upstream #3502 before publication.

Hermes-Card: t_a67bba0b4dbbb313
